sequenceDiagram
    participant A as Instance A (leader)
    participant B as Instance B (standby)
    participant C as Client C
    participant P as PgBouncer (transaction mode)
    participant S1 as Backend 1234
    participant S2 as Backend 5678

    A->>P: SELECT pg_try_advisory_lock(42)
    P->>S1: SELECT pg_try_advisory_lock(42)
    S1-->>A: true
    Note over A: Process killed, client connection drops
    Note over P,S1: Backend 1234 stays in the pool, still holding lock 42
    loop every few seconds
        B->>P: SELECT pg_try_advisory_lock(42)
        P->>S2: SELECT pg_try_advisory_lock(42)
        S2-->>B: false
    end
    C->>P: SELECT pg_try_advisory_lock(42)
    P->>S1: SELECT pg_try_advisory_lock(42)
    S1-->>C: true
    Note over P,S1: Released only when PgBouncer closes Backend 1234
